WEBVTT

00:05:59.453 --> 00:06:01.071
It's basically your IQ,

00:06:01.095 --> 00:06:03.880
your innate capacity
for learning and problem solving.

00:06:03.904 --> 00:06:06.721
AB: That's a big part
of the modern idea economy.

00:06:06.745 --> 00:06:08.030
I'm going to come in here,

00:06:08.054 --> 00:06:11.348
I'm going to be a whizzbang person
who comes up with brand new ideas.

00:06:11.372 --> 00:06:13.649
That's actually what's rewarded
for young people

00:06:13.673 --> 00:06:16.497
because young people
have high levels of fluid intelligence.

00:06:16.521 --> 00:06:19.071
It increases through your teens and 20s,

00:06:19.095 --> 00:06:20.428
and maybe through your 30s,

00:06:20.452 --> 00:06:23.960
although it tends to start declining
for most people in their 30s and 40s,

00:06:23.984 --> 00:06:27.102
and it makes this original
idea generation harder.

00:06:27.126 --> 00:06:29.896
Now that doesn't mean
that you're going to be unsuccessful,

00:06:29.920 --> 00:06:33.110
but it means if you're relying
entirely on this fluid intelligence,